# Example only. Nothing here is installed for you.
# Run `crontab -e` and adapt the paths. Mondays at 08:00 local time:
#
# 0 8 * * 1  cd ~/last30days-skill && \
#   python3 skills/last30days/scripts/watchlist.py run-all && \
#   python3 skills/last30days/scripts/briefing.py generate --weekly
#
# Notes from the last30days docs:
# - `watchlist.py add "<topic>" --weekly` only stores the schedule as metadata.
#   cron (or Task Scheduler on Windows) does the actual running.
# - Watchlist runs use --quick and a 90-day lookback.
# - The watchlist has a daily budget (default USD 5.00, counted in UTC).
#   Free sources cost nothing against it.
